sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Gate Admin
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (eu-ee31)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Admin->>+Gate: POST /gates/authorities
    Note over Admin,Gate: Authorization: Bearer admin-key<br/>Body: {"id":"aut-politsei-001","name":"Police and Border Guard Board","countryCode":"EE","subsets":["EU07","EU01"]}

    Gate->>Gate: Authenticate & authorize (role=ADMIN)

    Gate->>+DB: INSERT INTO authorities (id, name, countryCode, subsets)<br/>VALUES ('aut-politsei-001', 'Police and Border Guard Board', 'EE', '{EU07,full}')
    DB-->>-Gate: OK

    Gate-->>Admin: 200 OK\n{"id":"aut-politsei-001","name":"Police and Border Guard Board","countryCode":"EE","subsets":["EU07","EU01"]}

    Note over Admin: Authority registered with allowed subsets.<br/>Now create authority users.

    Admin->>+Gate: POST /users?generateSecret=true
    Note over Admin,Gate: Body: {"name":"Officer Jaan Tamm","email":"jaan.tamm@politsei.ee","roles":{"AUTHORITY":["aut-politsei-001"]},"subsets":["EU07"]}

    Gate->>Gate: Validate user subsets against authority subsets:<br/>user.subsets=["EU07"] ⊆ authority.subsets=["EU07","EU01"] → OK

    Gate->>Gate: Generate random secret

    Gate->>+DB: INSERT INTO users (name, email, roles, subsets, secretHash)<br/>VALUES ('Officer Jaan Tamm', 'jaan.tamm@politsei.ee',<br/>         '{"AUTHORITY":["aut-politsei-001"]}', '{EU07}', sha256hash(...))
    DB-->>-Gate: user.id="d2e3f4a5-..."

    Gate-->>-Admin: 200 OK\nd2e3f4a5-...:generated-secret-uuid

    Note over Admin: Authority user created with EU07 subset only.<br/>User can now call GET /identifiers and GET /dataset?subsetId=EU07

    alt Invalid subsets (user requests more than authority allows)
        Admin->>Gate: POST /users (subsets=["EU01"] but authority only has ["EU07"])
        Gate->>Gate: Validate: ["EU01"] ⊄ ["EU07"] → validation fails
        Gate-->>Admin: 400 Bad Request\n{"error": "Subsets must match Authority's subsets"}
    end
